<title>NETHERLANDS: Aegon seeks Frankfurt listing.</title>
<headline>Aegon seeks Frankfurt listing.</headline>
<dateline>THE HAGUE 1997-04-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Dutch insurer Aegon NV said on Tuesday it would seek a listing for its shares on the Frankfurt Stock Exchange.</p>
<p>&quot;The group has applied for a Frankfurt Stock Exchange listing to strengthen its presence in the German market,&quot; Aegon said in a statement.  </p>
<p>A spokesman for Aegon said no new shares would be issued for the official listing in Frankfurt. Deutsche Bank AG unit Deutsche Morgan Grenfell would act as Aegon's listing agent.</p>
<p>The application procedure is expected to be finalised within the next six weeks.</p>
<p>Aegon became active in Germany in 1995 when it set up Aegon Lebensversicherungs AG and started marketing savings products.</p>
<p>The company, one of the world's 10 largest independent listed insurers, is already listed in Amsterdam, London, New York, Zurich and Tokyo.</p>
<p>-- Amsterdam newsroom +31 20 504 5000, Fax +31 20 504 5040</p>
